{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And the seven empty ears</b> — Since the abundance in the land of Egypt is no great novelty, for it is like the garden of YHWH (Genesis 13:10), he mentioned first the interpretation of the years of famine, for that is the novelty and the benefit of the dream, since Elohim in His mercy showed Pharaoh the famine to sustain life through a great deliverance. And this is the meaning of \"and the seven years of famine began to come, according as Joseph had said\" (Genesis 41:54), for his word was not known except in the years of famine."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:43:25.611170356Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}